What is a Candlestick?

A candlestick represents the price movement of a stock during a specific time period (1 minute, 1 hour, 1 day, etc.).

Each candle shows 4 important values:

| Term  | Meaning                |
| ----- | ---------------------- |
| Open  | Price at the beginning |
| High  | Highest price reached  |
| Low   | Lowest price reached   |
| Close | Price at the end       |

